desc(
	mode: "source"
	language: "general"
	title: "Puppeteer Exposed Chrome Devtools"
	title_zh: "检测到 Puppeteer 暴露 Chrome 远程调试端口",
	type: vuln
	level: middle
	rule_id: "source-insecure-api-puppeteer-exposed-chrome-devtools"
	risk: "security-misconfiguration"
	desc: <<<DESC
Migrated from rule `puppeteer-exposed-chrome-devtools` (upstream/javascript/puppeteer/security/audit/puppeteer-exposed-chrome-devtools.yaml).
Original message: Remote debugging protocol does not perform any authentication, so exposing it too widely can be a security risk.

CWE: CWE-94: Improper Control of Generation of Code ('Code Injection')
References:
- https://owasp.org/Top10/A03_2021-Injection
Note: context-aware regex — remote debugging flags are kept only in files containing `require('puppeteer')`.
DESC
	solution: <<<SOLUTION
Do not expose Puppeteer's Chrome remote debugging endpoint broadly. Bind debugging ports to localhost or remove remote-debugging flags in untrusted contexts.
SOLUTION
	alert_min: 1
	"file://pos.js": <<<POS
const puppeteer = require('puppeteer');
const args = ['--remote-debugging-port=9222'];
POS
	"safefile://neg.js": <<<NEG
const puppeteer = require('puppeteer');
// no remote debugging flags
NEG
)

${*}.pattern_regex(/require\(\s*['"]puppeteer['"]\s*\)/) as $ctx
$ctx.regexp(/--remote-debugging-(?:address|port|socket-name|targets)/) as $hit
alert $hit for {
	level: "middle",
	title: "Puppeteer Exposed Chrome Devtools",
	title_zh: "检测到 Puppeteer 暴露 Chrome 远程调试端口",
	message: "Puppeteer remote debugging is exposed without authentication.",
}
